<title>UK: Iran, Nigeria tell OPEC they were on quota in Sept.</title>
<headline>Iran, Nigeria tell OPEC they were on quota in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran told OPEC it produced 3.598 million barrels per day (bpd) in September, just under its 3.67 million bpd quota, while Nigeria reported production at its 1.865 million bpd quota, the OPEC News Agency OPECNA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Of the other producers to have submitted production figures, Algeria and the UAE showed production above their respective quotas of 750,000 bpd and 2.161 million bpd.</p>
<p>Algeria showed production at 793,000 bpd and supply to market at 767,000 bpd. The UAE produced 2.189 million bpd and supplied 2.160 million bpd to the market.</p>
<p>OPEC quotas are determined according to market supply and not wellhead production. Supply, as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>All OPEC members except for Venezuela have submitted production data for September. Data received by the secretariat from member countries so far is as follows (in thousand bpd):  </p>
<p>			   PRODUCTION	    SUPPLY	OPEC QUOTA</p>
<p> ALGERIA		  793		    767	     750</p>
<p> INDONESIA	    1,326		    N/A	   1,330</p>
<p> IRAN		   3,598		  3,598	   3,600</p>
<p> IRAQ		     735		    735	   1,200</p>
<p> KUWAIT		 2,008.6		2,005.9	 2,000</p>
<p> LIBYA		  1,393.0		  N/A	   1,390</p>
<p> NIGERIA		1,865		  1,864.9	 1,865</p>
<p> QATAR		    394.1		  383.7	   378</p>
<p> SAUDI ARABIA	 8,059.5		8,003.6	 8,000</p>
<p> UAE		    2,189.4		2,160.8	 2,161</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
